      "hints": [
        "Find first term $a = u_1 = -6$ and common difference $d = u_2 - u_1 = -4.5 - (-6) = 1.5$.",
        "Set $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2(-6) + (n - 1)(1.5)] = 84$ and solve for integer $n$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the first two terms of the arithmetic progression from $u_n = \\frac{1}{2}(3n - 15)$:\n$$u_1 = a = \\frac{1}{2}(3(1) - 15) = \\frac{-12}{2} = -6$$\n$$u_2 = \\frac{1}{2}(3(2) - 15) = \\frac{-9}{2} = -4.5$$\n$$d = u_2 - u_1 = -4.5 - (-6) = 1.5 = \\frac{3}{2}$$",
        "Set up the sum equation $S_n = 84$ using $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2a + (n - 1)d]$:\n$$\\frac{n}{2}[2(-6) + (n - 1)(1.5)] = 84 \\implies \\frac{n}{2}[-12 + 1.5n - 1.5] = 84$$\n$$\\frac{n}{2}[1.5n - 13.5] = 84 \\implies n(1.5n - 13.5) = 168$$",
        "Multiply across by $2$ and form standard quadratic form:\n$$3n^2 - 27n - 336 = 0 \\implies n^2 - 9n - 112 = 0$$",
        "Factorise and solve for the positive integer $n$:\n$$(n - 16)(n + 7) = 0 \\implies n = 16 \\quad (\\text{rejecting } n = -7)$$"
      ],
